WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.872
Cleaning is not a collection of random fixes.

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:07.272
It is a sequence of evidence-based decisions.

00:00:07.272 --> 00:00:09.467
First, understand the source problems.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.407
Then apply only rules you can explain.

00:00:12.407 --> 00:00:15.432
Keep raw values when provenance matters.

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:20.942
And when the correct value is unknown, do not invent one.

00:00:20.942 --> 00:00:24.832
A review flag is often more honest than an automatic replacement.

00:00:24.832 --> 00:00:31.352
Connect this idea to a healthcare pipeline validating contact, demographic, and event fields.

00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:37.912
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:46.717
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:52.687
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:52.687 --> 00:00:58.656
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
